.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt IMP-SYSROOT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm imp-sysroot
.Nd fetch what a link for another system needs of that system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl fq
.Ar target ...
.Nm
.Fl Fl list
.Nm
.Fl Fl path Ar target
.Nm
.Fl Fl clean Op Ar target
.Nm
.Fl Fl apple-sdk Ar dir Ar target
.Nm
.Fl Fl readme Ar root
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
makes the files that
.Ql imp --target=TRIPLE
links with: the C library of the target system, its start files
.Pq Pa crt0.o , crt1.o , crtbegin.o ,
libm, libgcc or compiler-rt, its header files, and the runtime library of
.Xr imp 1
built for it, all in one directory laid out as
.Fl Fl sysroot
takes it.
The compiler calls it itself when
.Fl Fl target
is given with neither
.Fl Fl sysroot
nor
.Fl Fl runtime ;
the environment variable
.Ev IMPFETCH Ns =0
stops that.
.Pp
A
.Ar target
is a triple
.Pq Ql aarch64-linux-gnu , x86_64-linux-musl , x86_64-w64-mingw32 ,
or
.Ql OS/ARCH ,
and may end in
.Ql @release
for another release of a Linux distribution
.Pq Ql aarch64-linux-gnu@debian12 , x86_64-linux-musl@alpine321 .
.Fl Fl list
says which systems are known and which are here.
.Pp
The files are kept in
.Pa ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/imp/sysroots/OS[/RELEASE]/ARCH
.Pq Ev IMP_SYSROOTS
and nothing is installed or needs root.
They come, in this order, from the
.Sy sysroots
branch of the cruntime repository
.Pq Ev IMP_CRUNTIME , IMP_CRUNTIME_BRANCH ;
https://github.com/moebiusV/cruntime
and, where it has none, from the system's own packages: Debian's for glibc and mingw-w64,
Alpine's for musl, the base sets of FreeBSD, OpenBSD and NetBSD, Cygwin's, and, for macOS,
the SDK of a Mac
.Pq Fl Fl apple-sdk , or Xr xcrun 1
or the Darwin headers and libSystem stub of the Zig project's source tarball.
.Ev IMP_SYSROOT_SOURCE Ns =cruntime
or
.Ns =upstream
chooses one.
Each download is checked against the checksums of its index where there is one.
.Fl Fl readme
writes the provenance of every directory under a checkout of that branch into its README.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev IMP_SYSROOTS
the directory of the cache.
.It Ev IMP_CRUNTIME , IMP_CRUNTIME_BRANCH
the repository of the files and its branch.
.It Ev IMP_FREEBSD_VERSION , IMP_OPENBSD_VERSION , IMP_NETBSD_VERSION
a release of a BSD other than the newest.
.It Ev IMPFETCH
0 stops the compiler fetching.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa imp-meta
in each directory: what it was made from, with the SHA-256 sums.
.It Pa share/imp/sysroots.tsv
the table of systems and recipes.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 done, 1 failed, 2 usage or an unknown system, 3 macOS with no SDK to use.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr imp 1
.Sh AUTHORS
The imp authors.
